module

public import GroupDimension.TraceReplay.Magnus

@[expose] public section

/-!
# `ℤ[G]/Δⁿ` as a quotient of the truncated free algebra (fast-core paper, §3.1; MATH-306)

`cflint-fast-core`, `docs/analysis.md`, §3.1 (with the proof of §3.2):

> Let `G = F/N`, `π : ℤ[F] → ℤ[G]`, `𝔯 = ker π`, and let `μ : ℤ[F] → A_n` be the Magnus ring
> homomorphism `x_i ↦ 1 + a_i`. Let `R₀ ⊂ F` normally generate `N`.
> **Theorem.** `ℤ[G]/Δⁿ ≅ A_n/J_n`, where `J_n = span_ℤ{u (μ(r) − 1) v : r ∈ R₀; u, v monomials}`
> is the two-sided ideal generated by the elements `μ(r) − 1`. The isomorphism sends `g` to
> `μ(w_g)` for any word `w_g` representing `g`. Therefore `g ∈ D_n(G) ⟺ μ(w_g) − 1 ∈ J_n`.
> Moreover, `A_n⁺/J_n ≅ Δ/Δⁿ` is a finite `p`-group …

## Setting

* `X` is any type (the generators), `F = FreeGroup X`, `ZF X = ℤ[F]`, and `FA X = ℤ⟨a⟩ =
  MonoidAlgebra ℤ (FreeMonoid X)` the free associative ring on letters `a_x`, `x : X` (words are its
  `ℤ`-basis). `Ik X k` is the span of the words of length `≥ k`, `Itr X k` the same set as a
  two-sided ideal, and `A X n = ℤ⟨a⟩ / Itr X n` is the truncated algebra `A_n`.
* `muF n : F →* A_nˣ`, `x ↦ 1 + a_x`, and its linear extension `mu n : ℤ[F] →+* A_n` (the paper's `μ`).
  `Pk n k` is the image of `Ik X k` in `A_n`; `Pk n 1` is the paper's `A_n⁺`.
* `G` is any group with a surjection `φ : F →* G` whose kernel is the normal closure of `R0 : Set F`
  (`hφ`, `hker`); `π = mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ : ℤ[F] →+* ℤ[G]`. The presented group
  `PresentedGroup R0` is the special case `φ = PresentedGroup.mk R0` (`*_presented`).
* `relIdeal R0 ⊆ ℤ[F]` is `span_ℤ{u (r − 1) v : r ∈ R0, u, v ∈ F}`, a two-sided ideal, the smallest
  one containing all `r − 1` (`relIdeal_le`). `Jspan R0 n ⊆ A_n` is the paper's
  `J_n = span_ℤ{u (μ(r) − 1) v : r ∈ R0, u, v words}`, and `Jideal R0 n` the same set as a two-sided
  ideal of `A_n`.
* `augIdeal`, `augmentation` and `D n G = {g | g − 1 ∈ Δⁿ}` are those of `GroupDimension.Basic`.

## What is proved

* (a) `magnusEquiv n : ℤ[F] ⧸ 𝔣ⁿ ≃+* A_n`, with `magnusEquiv_mk_of : g ↦ μ(g)`; the inverse is
  induced by `psi : ℤ⟨a⟩ →+* ℤ[F]`, `a_x ↦ x − 1` (`psi_Ik`, `mu_psi`, `phibar_mu`). Also
  `mu_sub_aug_mem` (the constant term of `μ(f)` is `ε(f)`), `ker_mu`.
* (b) `ker_pi_eq : ker π = relIdeal R0`, i.e. `ker π` is the two-sided ideal generated by the
  `r − 1`, `r ∈ R0` (`sub_one_mem_relIdeal`, `relIdeal_le`); `ker_pi_presented` for
  `PresentedGroup R0`.
* (c) `mem_Jideal_iff : y ∈ J_n ⟺ y ∈ μ(relIdeal R0)` (`J_n = μ(𝔯)`), the two kernels
  `ker_PsiG : ker(ℤ[F] → ℤ[G]/Δⁿ) = 𝔯 + 𝔣ⁿ` (with `exists_lift_pow`: `π(𝔣ᵏ) = Δᵏ`) and
  `ker_PhiA : ker(ℤ[F] → A_n/J_n) = 𝔯 + 𝔣ⁿ`, and the isomorphism
  `quotEquiv : ℤ[G] ⧸ Δⁿ ≃+* A_n ⧸ J_n` with `quotEquiv_mk_of : φ w ↦ μ(w)`.
  The corollary `mem_D_iff : φ w ∈ D_n(G) ⟺ μ(w) − 1 ∈ J_n`, and `mem_D_presented`.
* (d) `finite_augQuot`: for `G` finite, `Δ/Δⁿ` (as the abelian group `augQuot G n`) is finite
  (it is killed by `|G|^{n−1}`); `pow_smul_aug_mem_of_exponent`: if the exponent of `G` divides
  `p^N` (e.g. `G` a finite `p`-group, `exponent_of_isPGroup`), then `p^{N(n−1)} Δ ⊆ Δⁿ`;
  `augQuot_isPGroup`: for a finite `p`-group, `Δ/Δⁿ` is finite and killed by a power of `p`, i.e. a
  finite `p`-group. The route differs from the paper's (which uses
  `(Δ/Δ²)^{⊗k} ↠ Δᵏ/Δᵏ⁺¹`): it uses `q^j Δ ⊆ Δ^{j+1}` when `x^q = 1` (`TraceReplay.pow_smul_mem`).
  On the `A_n` side
  `pow_smul_pos_mem_J`: `q^{n−1} A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n` when `x^q = 1` on `G`. Exactness modulo a power of `p`:
  `exact_of_bounded` (abstract) and `exact_mod_p` / `mem_J_iff_mod_p`: if the exponent of `G`
  divides `p^N` and `p^E A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺`, then `p^E A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n`, and for `y ∈ A_n⁺`,
  `y ∈ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺ ⟺ y ∈ J_n` (the paper's `E` is our `E + 1`). Non-membership modulo
  `p^{E+1}` is exact for free (`J_n ⊆ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺`). End to end, `mem_D_iff_mod_p`:
  `φ w ∈ D_n(G) ⟺ μ(w) − 1 ∈ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺` under the same hypotheses.

## What is not formalized here (the gap to the paper)

* The additive isomorphism `A_n⁺/J_n ≅ Δ/Δⁿ` is not stated as an equivalence of groups; it is the
  restriction of `quotEquiv` to the augmentation parts, and what the exactness argument needs from
  it (`q^{n−1} A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n`) is proved directly (`pow_smul_pos_mem_J`).
* `ε(J_n) = 0` (i.e. `J_n ⊆ A_n⁺`) and the splitting `A_n = ℤ ⊕ A_n⁺` are not stated; the
  exactness argument does not need them.
* The equality of the `index_logp` fields (`log_p |A_n⁺/(J_n + p^E A_n⁺)| = log_p |Δ/(Δⁿ + p^E Δ)|`)
  and `rk A_n⁺ = M` independent of `|G|` are not stated.
* (b′) (a right ideal suffices for Schreier generators) and §3.3–3.4 (where the relations come from,
  all levels at once) are not formalized; nor is anything about the programs `magnus.py`,
  `magnus_pres.py` or their Howell forms.
-/

namespace GroupDimension.Kernel.Magnus

noncomputable section

open MonoidAlgebra

variable {X : Type*}

/-- `ℤ⟨a⟩`: the free associative ring on the letters `a_x`, `x : X`; words are its `ℤ`-basis. -/
abbrev FA (X : Type*) := MonoidAlgebra ℤ (FreeMonoid X)

/-- `ℤ[F]`: the integral group ring of the free group on `X`. -/
abbrev ZF (X : Type*) := MonoidAlgebra ℤ (FreeGroup X)

/-! ## The truncation ideal and `A_n` -/

variable (X) in
/-- The span of the words of length `≥ k`. -/
def Ik (k : ℕ) : Submodule ℤ (FA X) :=
  Submodule.span ℤ {x | ∃ w : FreeMonoid X, k ≤ w.length ∧ x = single w 1}

theorem single_eq_smul (m : FreeMonoid X) (r : ℤ) : (single m r : FA X) = r • single m 1 := by
  rw [smul_single', mul_one]

theorem single_mem_Ik {k : ℕ} {w : FreeMonoid X} (hw : k ≤ w.length) (a : ℤ) :
    (single w a : FA X) ∈ Ik X k := by
  rw [single_eq_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a (Submodule.subset_span ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩)

theorem Ik_mono {k k' : ℕ} (h : k ≤ k') : Ik X k' ≤ Ik X k :=
  Submodule.span_mono fun _ ⟨w, hw, hx⟩ => ⟨w, by omega, hx⟩

theorem mem_Ik_zero (x : FA X) : x ∈ Ik X 0 := by
  induction x using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add f g hf hg => exact add_mem hf hg
  | single m r => exact single_mem_Ik (Nat.zero_le _) r

/-- `u · I_k · v ⊆ I_{k + |u| + |v|}`. -/
theorem single_mul_mem_Ik {k : ℕ} {x : FA X} (hx : x ∈ Ik X k) (u v : FreeMonoid X) :
    single u 1 * x * single v 1 ∈ Ik X (k + u.length + v.length) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩ := hx
    rw [single_mul_single, single_mul_single]
    exact single_mem_Ik (by simp only [FreeMonoid.length_mul]; omega) _
  | zero => simp
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [mul_add, add_mul]; exact add_mem hx hy
  | smul a x _ hx => rw [mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a hx

theorem mul_mem_Ik {k : ℕ} {x : FA X} (hx : x ∈ Ik X k) (y : FA X) : x * y ∈ Ik X k := by
  induction y using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add f g hf hg => rw [mul_add]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | single m r =>
    rw [single_eq_smul, mul_smul_comm]
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ r ?_
    have h := single_mul_mem_Ik hx 1 m
    rw [← one_def, one_mul] at h
    exact Ik_mono (by omega) h

theorem mem_Ik_mul {k : ℕ} {x : FA X} (hx : x ∈ Ik X k) (y : FA X) : y * x ∈ Ik X k := by
  induction y using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp
  | add f g hf hg => rw [add_mul]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | single m r =>
    rw [single_eq_smul, smul_mul_assoc]
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ r ?_
    have h := single_mul_mem_Ik hx m 1
    rw [← one_def, mul_one] at h
    exact Ik_mono (by omega) h

/-- `I_i · I_j ⊆ I_{i+j}`. -/
theorem mul_mem_Ik_add {i j : ℕ} {x y : FA X} (hx : x ∈ Ik X i) (hy : y ∈ Ik X j) :
    x * y ∈ Ik X (i + j) := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem a ha =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩ := ha
    induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem b hb =>
      obtain ⟨v, hv, rfl⟩ := hb
      rw [single_mul_single, one_mul]
      exact single_mem_Ik (by rw [FreeMonoid.length_mul]; omega) _
    | zero => rw [mul_zero]; exact zero_mem _
    | add b c _ _ hb hc => rw [mul_add]; exact add_mem hb hc
    | smul c b _ hb => rw [mul_smul_comm]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c hb
  | zero => rw [zero_mul]; exact zero_mem _
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [add_mul]; exact add_mem ha hb
  | smul c a _ ha => rw [smul_mul_assoc]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c ha

variable (X) in
/-- `I_k` as a two-sided ideal of `ℤ⟨a⟩`. -/
def Itr (k : ℕ) : Ideal (FA X) where
  carrier := Ik X k
  add_mem' := add_mem
  zero_mem' := zero_mem _
  smul_mem' c _ hx := mem_Ik_mul hx c

instance Itr_isTwoSided (k : ℕ) : (Itr X k).IsTwoSided := ⟨fun b ha => mul_mem_Ik ha b⟩

theorem mem_Itr {k : ℕ} {x : FA X} : x ∈ Itr X k ↔ x ∈ Ik X k := Iff.rfl

variable (X) in
/-- The truncated free algebra `A_n = ℤ⟨a⟩ / (words of length ≥ n)`. -/
abbrev A (n : ℕ) := FA X ⧸ Itr X n

/-- The image in `A_n` of a word. -/
abbrev mon (n : ℕ) (u : FreeMonoid X) : A X n := Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X n) (single u 1)

theorem mon_mul (n : ℕ) (u v : FreeMonoid X) : mon n (u * v) = mon n u * mon n v := by
  rw [mon, mon, mon, ← map_mul, single_mul_single, one_mul]

theorem mon_one (n : ℕ) : mon n (1 : FreeMonoid X) = 1 := by
  rw [mon, ← one_def, map_one]

/-- The letter `a_x ∈ A_n`. -/
abbrev aA (n : ℕ) (j : X) : A X n := mon n (FreeMonoid.of j)

theorem length_pow_of (l : X) (m : ℕ) : (FreeMonoid.of l ^ m).length = m := by
  induction m with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ m ih => rw [pow_succ, FreeMonoid.length_mul, ih, FreeMonoid.length_of]

theorem isNilpotent_aA (n : ℕ) (j : X) : IsNilpotent (aA n j) := by
  refine ⟨n, ?_⟩
  rw [aA, mon, ← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, mem_Itr, single_pow, one_pow]
  exact single_mem_Ik (le_of_eq (length_pow_of j n).symm) _

/-- `1 + a_x` as a unit of `A_n`. -/
def unitA (n : ℕ) (j : X) : (A X n)ˣ := (isNilpotent_aA n j).isUnit_one_add.unit

/-- The Magnus map `F → A_nˣ`, `x ↦ 1 + a_x`. -/
def muF (n : ℕ) : FreeGroup X →* (A X n)ˣ := FreeGroup.lift (unitA n)

theorem muF_of (n : ℕ) (j : X) : (muF n (FreeGroup.of j) : A X n) = 1 + aA n j := by
  rw [muF, FreeGroup.lift_apply_of, unitA, IsUnit.unit_spec]

/-- The Magnus ring homomorphism `μ : ℤ[F] → A_n`. -/
def mu (n : ℕ) : ZF X →+* A X n :=
  liftNCRingHom (Int.castRingHom (A X n)) ((Units.coeHom (A X n)).comp (muF n))
    (fun c _ => Int.cast_commute c _)

theorem mu_single (n : ℕ) (g : FreeGroup X) (c : ℤ) :
    mu n (single g c) = (c : A X n) * (muF n g : A X n) := by
  rw [mu, liftNCRingHom_single]; rfl

theorem mu_of (n : ℕ) (g : FreeGroup X) : mu n (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) g) = (muF n g : A X n) := by
  rw [of_apply, mu_single, Int.cast_one, one_mul]

theorem mu_sub_one (n : ℕ) (g : FreeGroup X) :
    mu n (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) g - 1) = (muF n g : A X n) - 1 := by
  rw [map_sub, map_one, mu_of]

/-! ## `A_n⁺` and its powers -/

/-- The image of `I_k` in `A_n`; `Pk n 1` is `A_n⁺`. -/
def Pk (n k : ℕ) : Submodule ℤ (A X n) where
  carrier := {y | ∃ x ∈ Ik X k, Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X n) x = y}
  add_mem' := by
    rintro _ _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨x + y, add_mem hx hy, map_add _ _ _⟩
  zero_mem' := ⟨0, zero_mem _, map_zero _⟩
  smul_mem' := by
    rintro c _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨c • x, Submodule.smul_mem _ c hx, map_zsmul _ c x⟩

theorem mem_Pk {n k : ℕ} {y : A X n} :
    y ∈ Pk n k ↔ ∃ x ∈ Ik X k, Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X n) x = y := Iff.rfl

theorem mem_Pk_zero (n : ℕ) (y : A X n) : y ∈ Pk n 0 := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
  exact mem_Pk.mpr ⟨x, mem_Ik_zero x, rfl⟩

theorem Pk_mul {n i j : ℕ} {a b : A X n} (ha : a ∈ Pk n i) (hb : b ∈ Pk n j) :
    a * b ∈ Pk n (i + j) := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := mem_Pk.mp ha
  obtain ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ := mem_Pk.mp hb
  exact mem_Pk.mpr ⟨x * y, mul_mem_Ik_add hx hy, map_mul _ _ _⟩

theorem eq_zero_of_mem_Pk_self {n : ℕ} {y : A X n} (hy : y ∈ Pk n n) : y = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := mem_Pk.mp hy
  exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hx

theorem muF_sub_one_mem (n : ℕ) (g : FreeGroup X) : (muF n g : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1 := by
  let T : Subgroup (FreeGroup X) :=
    { carrier := {g | (muF n g : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1}
      mul_mem' := by
        intro x y hx hy
        have hx' : (muF n x : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1 := hx
        have hy' : (muF n y : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1 := hy
        obtain ⟨a, ha, ea⟩ := mem_Pk.mp hx'
        obtain ⟨b, hb, eb⟩ := mem_Pk.mp hy'
        show (muF n (x * y) : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1
        refine mem_Pk.mpr ⟨a * b + a + b, add_mem (add_mem (mul_mem_Ik ha b) ha) hb, ?_⟩
        rw [map_add, map_add, map_mul, ea, eb, map_mul, Units.val_mul]; noncomm_ring
      one_mem' := by
        show (muF (X := X) n 1 : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1
        rw [map_one, Units.val_one, sub_self]; exact zero_mem _
      inv_mem' := by
        intro x hx
        have hx' : (muF n x : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1 := hx
        obtain ⟨a, ha, ea⟩ := mem_Pk.mp hx'
        obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (muF n x⁻¹ : A X n)
        show (muF n x⁻¹ : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1
        refine mem_Pk.mpr ⟨-(c * a), neg_mem (mem_Ik_mul ha c), ?_⟩
        rw [map_neg, map_mul, hc, ea, map_inv, mul_sub, Units.inv_mul, mul_one]; abel }
  have hgen : ∀ j, FreeGroup.of j ∈ T := fun j => by
    show (muF n (FreeGroup.of j) : A X n) - 1 ∈ Pk n 1
    rw [muF_of, add_sub_cancel_left]
    exact mem_Pk.mpr ⟨single (FreeMonoid.of j) 1, single_mem_Ik (by simp) _, rfl⟩
  have hT : T = ⊤ := by
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← FreeGroup.closure_range_of, Subgroup.closure_le]
    rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩; exact hgen j
  have : g ∈ T := hT ▸ Subgroup.mem_top g
  exact this

theorem augmentation_single {G : Type*} [Group G] (g : G) (c : ℤ) :
    augmentation G (single g c) = c := by
  rw [show (single g c : MonoidAlgebra ℤ G) = c • of ℤ G g by rw [of_apply, smul_single', mul_one],
    map_zsmul, augmentation_of, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]

/-- The constant term of `μ(f)` is the augmentation `ε(f)`: `μ(f) − ε(f) ∈ A_n⁺`. -/
theorem mu_sub_aug_mem (n : ℕ) (x : ZF X) :
    mu n x - ((augmentation (FreeGroup X) x : ℤ) : A X n) ∈ Pk n 1 := by
  induction x using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, map_zero, Int.cast_zero, sub_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add x y hx hy =>
    rw [map_add, map_add, Int.cast_add]
    convert add_mem hx hy using 1; abel
  | single g c =>
    rw [mu_single, augmentation_single,
      show (c : A X n) * (muF n g : A X n) - c = c • ((muF n g : A X n) - 1) by
        rw [zsmul_eq_mul, mul_sub, mul_one]]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c (muF_sub_one_mem n g)

theorem mu_aug_mem (n : ℕ) {x : ZF X} (hx : x ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X)) : mu n x ∈ Pk n 1 := by
  have h := mu_sub_aug_mem n x
  rwa [mem_augIdeal.mp hx, Int.cast_zero, sub_zero] at h

/-- `μ(𝔣ᵏ) ⊆ (A_n⁺)ᵏ`. -/
theorem mu_pow_mem (n : ℕ) : ∀ k : ℕ, ∀ x ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ k, mu n x ∈ Pk n k
  | 0, x, _ => mem_Pk_zero n (mu n x)
  | k + 1, x, hx => by
    rw [Submodule.pow_succ] at hx
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hx (fun a ha b hb => ?_) (fun a b ha hb => ?_)
    · rw [map_mul]; exact Pk_mul (mu_pow_mem n k a ha) (mu_aug_mem n hb)
    · rw [map_add]; exact add_mem ha hb

theorem mu_eq_zero_of_mem {n : ℕ} {x : ZF X} (hx : x ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n) : mu n x = 0 :=
  eq_zero_of_mem_Pk_self (mu_pow_mem n n x hx)

/-- `μ̄ : ℤ[F]/𝔣ⁿ → A_n`. -/
def mubar (n : ℕ) : ZF X ⧸ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n →+* A X n :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift _ (mu n) (fun _ h => mu_eq_zero_of_mem h)

theorem mubar_mk (n : ℕ) (x : ZF X) : mubar n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) = mu n x := rfl

/-! ## The inverse: `a_x ↦ x − 1` -/

/-- `ψ : ℤ⟨a⟩ → ℤ[F]`, `a_x ↦ x − 1`. -/
def psi : FA X →+* ZF X :=
  liftNCRingHom (Int.castRingHom (ZF X))
    (FreeMonoid.lift fun j => of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (FreeGroup.of j) - 1)
    (fun c _ => Int.cast_commute c _)

theorem psi_single (w : FreeMonoid X) (c : ℤ) :
    psi (single w c) = (c : ZF X) *
      (w.toList.map fun j => of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (FreeGroup.of j) - 1).prod := by
  rw [psi, liftNCRingHom_single, FreeMonoid.lift_apply]; rfl

theorem psi_letter (j : X) :
    psi (single (FreeMonoid.of j) 1) = of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (FreeGroup.of j) - 1 := by
  rw [psi_single, FreeMonoid.toList_of, List.map_singleton, List.prod_singleton, Int.cast_one,
    one_mul]

theorem psi_single_mem (w : FreeMonoid X) (c : ℤ) :
    psi (single w c) ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ w.length := by
  rw [psi_single]
  refine Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ ?_
  have := TraceReplay.list_prod_mem_pow
    (w.toList.map fun j => of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (FreeGroup.of j) - 1) (fun x hx => by
      obtain ⟨j, -, rfl⟩ := List.mem_map.mp hx
      exact of_sub_one_mem_augIdeal _)
  rw [List.length_map] at this
  exact this

/-- `ψ(I_k) ⊆ 𝔣ᵏ`. -/
theorem psi_Ik {k : ℕ} {x : FA X} (hx : x ∈ Ik X k) : psi x ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ k := by
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨w, hw, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact Ideal.pow_le_pow_right hw (psi_single_mem w 1)
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem hx hy
  | smul c x _ hx => rw [map_zsmul]; exact zsmul_mem hx c

/-- `φ̄ : A_n → ℤ[F]/𝔣ⁿ`, `a_x ↦ x − 1`. -/
def phibar (n : ℕ) : A X n →+* ZF X ⧸ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n :=
  Ideal.Quotient.lift (Itr X n) ((Ideal.Quotient.mk _).comp psi) (fun a ha => by
    rw [RingHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact psi_Ik (mem_Itr.mp ha))

theorem phibar_mk (n : ℕ) (x : FA X) :
    phibar n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (psi x) := rfl

/-- `μ ∘ ψ` is the quotient map `ℤ⟨a⟩ → A_n`. -/
theorem mu_psi (n : ℕ) (x : FA X) : mu n (psi x) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X n) x := by
  have h : (mu n).comp (psi (X := X)) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X n) := by
    refine MonoidAlgebra.ringHom_ext' (RingHom.ext_int _ _) (FreeMonoid.hom_eq fun j => ?_)
    show mu n (psi (single (FreeMonoid.of j) 1)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X n) (single (FreeMonoid.of j) 1)
    rw [psi_letter, mu_sub_one, muF_of, add_sub_cancel_left]
  exact RingHom.congr_fun h x

set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 200000 in
/-- `φ̄ ∘ μ` is the quotient map `ℤ[F] → ℤ[F]/𝔣ⁿ`. -/
theorem phibar_mu (n : ℕ) (x : ZF X) :
    phibar n (mu n x) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n) x := by
  have h : (phibar n).comp (mu n) = Ideal.Quotient.mk (augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n) := by
    refine MonoidAlgebra.ringHom_ext' (RingHom.ext_int _ _) (FreeGroup.ext_hom _ _ fun j => ?_)
    show phibar n (mu n (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (FreeGroup.of j))) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (FreeGroup.of j))
    rw [mu_of, muF_of, map_add, map_one, aA, mon, phibar_mk, psi_letter, map_sub, map_one]
    abel
  exact RingHom.congr_fun h x

/-- **(a) The truncated Magnus isomorphism** `ℤ[F]/𝔣ⁿ ≅ A_n`. -/
def magnusEquiv (n : ℕ) : ZF X ⧸ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n ≃+* A X n :=
  RingEquiv.ofRingHom (mubar n) (phibar n)
    (RingHom.ext fun y => by
      obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
      rw [RingHom.comp_apply, phibar_mk, mubar_mk, mu_psi, RingHom.id_apply])
    (RingHom.ext fun y => by
      obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
      rw [RingHom.comp_apply, mubar_mk, phibar_mu, RingHom.id_apply])

theorem magnusEquiv_mk (n : ℕ) (x : ZF X) :
    magnusEquiv n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) = mu n x := rfl

theorem magnusEquiv_mk_of (n : ℕ) (g : FreeGroup X) :
    magnusEquiv n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) g)) = (muF n g : A X n) := by
  rw [magnusEquiv_mk, mu_of]

/-- `ker μ = 𝔣ⁿ`. -/
theorem ker_mu (n : ℕ) : RingHom.ker (mu (X := X) n) = augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n := by
  ext x
  rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
  constructor
  · intro h
    rw [← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, ← phibar_mu, h, map_zero]
  · exact mu_eq_zero_of_mem

theorem mu_surjective (n : ℕ) : Function.Surjective (mu (X := X) n) := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
  exact ⟨psi x, mu_psi n x⟩

/-! ## (b) The kernel of `ℤ[F] → ℤ[G]` -/

/-- `span_ℤ {u (r − 1) v : r ∈ R0, u, v ∈ F}`. -/
def relSpan (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)) : Submodule ℤ (ZF X) :=
  Submodule.span ℤ {x | ∃ r ∈ R0, ∃ u v : FreeGroup X,
    x = of ℤ (FreeGroup X) u * (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) r - 1) * of ℤ (FreeGroup X) v}

theorem single_eq_smul_of {G : Type*} [Group G] (g : G) (c : ℤ) :
    (single g c : MonoidAlgebra ℤ G) = c • of ℤ G g := by
  rw [of_apply, smul_single', mul_one]

theorem relSpan_mul_left (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)) (y : ZF X) {x : ZF X} (hx : x ∈ relSpan R0) :
    y * x ∈ relSpan R0 := by
  induction y using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => rw [zero_mul]; exact zero_mem _
  | add f g hf hg => rw [add_mul]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | single g c =>
    rw [single_eq_smul_of, smul_mul_assoc]
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ c ?_
    induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, u, v, rfl⟩ := hx
      refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, g * u, v, ?_⟩
      rw [map_mul]; noncomm_ring
    | zero => rw [mul_zero]; exact zero_mem _
    | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [mul_add]; exact add_mem ha hb
    | smul c' a _ ha => rw [mul_smul_comm]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c' ha

theorem relSpan_mul_right (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)) (y : ZF X) {x : ZF X} (hx : x ∈ relSpan R0) :
    x * y ∈ relSpan R0 := by
  induction y using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => rw [mul_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add f g hf hg => rw [mul_add]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | single g c =>
    rw [single_eq_smul_of, mul_smul_comm]
    refine Submodule.smul_mem _ c ?_
    induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, u, v, rfl⟩ := hx
      refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, u, v * g, ?_⟩
      rw [map_mul]; noncomm_ring
    | zero => rw [zero_mul]; exact zero_mem _
    | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [add_mul]; exact add_mem ha hb
    | smul c' a _ ha => rw [smul_mul_assoc]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c' ha

/-- The two-sided ideal of `ℤ[F]` generated by the `r − 1`, `r ∈ R0`. -/
def relIdeal (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)) : Ideal (ZF X) where
  carrier := relSpan R0
  add_mem' := add_mem
  zero_mem' := zero_mem _
  smul_mem' c _ hx := relSpan_mul_left R0 c hx

instance relIdeal_isTwoSided (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)) : (relIdeal R0).IsTwoSided :=
  ⟨fun b ha => relSpan_mul_right R0 b ha⟩

theorem mem_relIdeal {R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)} {x : ZF X} : x ∈ relIdeal R0 ↔ x ∈ relSpan R0 :=
  Iff.rfl

theorem sub_one_mem_relIdeal {R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)} {r : FreeGroup X} (hr : r ∈ R0) :
    of ℤ (FreeGroup X) r - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0 :=
  mem_relIdeal.mpr (Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, 1, 1, by rw [map_one, one_mul, mul_one]⟩)

/-- `relIdeal R0` is the smallest two-sided ideal containing all `r − 1`. -/
theorem relIdeal_le {R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)} (I : Ideal (ZF X)) [I.IsTwoSided]
    (h : ∀ r ∈ R0, of ℤ (FreeGroup X) r - 1 ∈ I) : relIdeal R0 ≤ I := by
  intro x hx
  rw [mem_relIdeal] at hx
  induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx =>
    obtain ⟨r, hr, u, v, rfl⟩ := hx
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (h r hr))
  | zero => exact zero_mem _
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => exact add_mem ha hb
  | smul c a _ ha => exact zsmul_mem ha c

/-- `n − 1 ∈ relIdeal R0` for every `n` in the normal closure of `R0`. -/
theorem sub_one_mem_of_mem_normalClosure {R0 : Set (FreeGroup X)} {w : FreeGroup X}
    (hw : w ∈ Subgroup.normalClosure R0) : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) w - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0 := by
  let T : Subgroup (FreeGroup X) :=
    { carrier := {w | of ℤ (FreeGroup X) w - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0}
      one_mem' := by
        show of ℤ (FreeGroup X) 1 - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0
        rw [map_one, sub_self]; exact zero_mem _
      mul_mem' := by
        intro a b ha hb
        have ha' : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0 := ha
        have hb' : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) b - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0 := hb
        show of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (a * b) - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0
        have e : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (a * b) - 1 =
            (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a - 1) * of ℤ (FreeGroup X) b + (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) b - 1) := by
          rw [map_mul]; noncomm_ring
        rw [e]
        exact add_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ ha') hb'
      inv_mem' := by
        intro a ha
        have ha' : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0 := ha
        show of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a⁻¹ - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0
        have e : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a⁻¹ - 1 =
            -((of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a - 1) * of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a⁻¹) := by
          have hh : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a * of ℤ (FreeGroup X) a⁻¹ = 1 := by
            rw [← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel, map_one]
          rw [sub_mul, hh]; noncomm_ring
        rw [e]
        exact neg_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ ha') }
  have hT : T.Normal := ⟨fun g hg h => by
    have hg' : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) g - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0 := hg
    show of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (h * g * h⁻¹) - 1 ∈ relIdeal R0
    have e : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (h * g * h⁻¹) - 1 =
        of ℤ (FreeGroup X) h * (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) g - 1) * of ℤ (FreeGroup X) h⁻¹ := by
      have hh : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) h * of ℤ (FreeGroup X) h⁻¹ = 1 := by
        rw [← map_mul, mul_inv_cancel, map_one]
      rw [map_mul, map_mul, mul_sub, sub_mul, mul_one, hh]
    rw [e]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hg')⟩
  have hle : Subgroup.normalClosure R0 ≤ T :=
    Subgroup.normalClosure_le_normal (fun r hr => sub_one_mem_relIdeal hr)
  exact hle hw

section Group

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] (φ : FreeGroup X →* G) (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X))

theorem pi_single (g : FreeGroup X) (c : ℤ) :
    mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ (single g c) = single (φ g) c := by
  rw [mapDomainRingHom_apply, mapDomain_single]

theorem pi_of (g : FreeGroup X) :
    mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) g) = of ℤ G (φ g) := by
  rw [of_apply, of_apply, pi_single]

theorem aug_pi (x : ZF X) :
    augmentation G (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ x) = augmentation (FreeGroup X) x := by
  induction x using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => simp only [map_zero]
  | add x y hx hy => simp only [map_add, hx, hy]
  | single g c => rw [pi_single, augmentation_single, augmentation_single]

theorem pi_surjective (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) :
    Function.Surjective (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ) := by
  intro z
  induction z using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => exact ⟨0, map_zero _⟩
  | add a b ha hb =>
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := ha
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hb
    exact ⟨x + y, by rw [map_add, hx, hy]⟩
  | single g c =>
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hφ g
    exact ⟨single w c, by rw [pi_single, hw]⟩

/-- **(b)** `ker π` is the two-sided ideal generated by the `r − 1`, `r ∈ R0`. -/
theorem ker_pi_eq (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0) :
    RingHom.ker (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ) = relIdeal R0 := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · intro x hx
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker] at hx
    obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ : ∃ s : G → FreeGroup X, ∀ g, φ (s g) = g := ⟨_, Function.surjInv_eq hφ⟩
    have key : ∀ y : ZF X,
        y - mapDomain s (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ y) ∈ relIdeal R0 := by
      intro y
      induction y using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
      | zero => rw [map_zero, mapDomain_zero, sub_zero]; exact zero_mem _
      | add a b ha hb =>
        rw [map_add, mapDomain_add]
        convert add_mem ha hb using 1; abel
      | single g c =>
        rw [pi_single, mapDomain_single]
        have hn : (s (φ g))⁻¹ * g ∈ Subgroup.normalClosure R0 := by
          rw [← hker, MonoidHom.mem_ker, map_mul, map_inv, hs, inv_mul_cancel]
        have e : (single g c : ZF X) - single (s (φ g)) c =
            c • (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) (s (φ g)) *
              (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) ((s (φ g))⁻¹ * g) - 1)) := by
          rw [mul_sub, ← map_mul (of ℤ (FreeGroup X)), mul_inv_cancel_left, mul_one, smul_sub,
            single_eq_smul_of g c, single_eq_smul_of (s (φ g)) c]
        rw [e]
        exact zsmul_mem (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (sub_one_mem_of_mem_normalClosure hn)) c
    have := key x
    rwa [hx, mapDomain_zero, sub_zero] at this
  · refine relIdeal_le _ fun r hr => ?_
    have h1 : φ r = 1 := by
      rw [← MonoidHom.mem_ker, hker]; exact Subgroup.subset_normalClosure hr
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, map_one, pi_of, h1, map_one, sub_self]

/-- **(b)** for the presented group `⟨X | R0⟩`. -/
theorem ker_pi_presented :
    RingHom.ker (mapDomainRingHom ℤ (PresentedGroup.mk R0)) = relIdeal R0 :=
  ker_pi_eq _ R0 (PresentedGroup.mk_surjective R0)
    (by ext x; exact MonoidHom.mem_ker.trans PresentedGroup.mk_eq_one_iff)

/-! ## (c) Putting it together -/

/-- `π(𝔣ᵏ) ⊆ Δᵏ`. -/
theorem pi_pow_mem : ∀ k : ℕ, ∀ y ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ k,
    mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ y ∈ augIdeal G ^ k
  | 0, y, _ => by simp [Submodule.pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
  | k + 1, y, hy => by
    rw [Submodule.pow_succ] at hy
    rw [Submodule.pow_succ]
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hy (fun a ha b hb => ?_) (fun a b ha hb => ?_)
    · rw [map_mul]
      refine Submodule.mul_mem_mul (pi_pow_mem k a ha) ?_
      rw [mem_augIdeal, aug_pi]; exact mem_augIdeal.mp hb
    · rw [map_add]; exact add_mem ha hb

/-- `Δᵏ ⊆ π(𝔣ᵏ)` for surjective `φ`. -/
theorem exists_lift_pow (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) : ∀ k : ℕ, ∀ z ∈ augIdeal G ^ k,
    ∃ y ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ k, mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ y = z
  | 0, z, _ => by
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := pi_surjective φ hφ z
    exact ⟨y, by simp [Submodule.pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top], hy⟩
  | k + 1, z, hz => by
    rw [Submodule.pow_succ] at hz
    refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hz (fun a ha b hb => ?_) (fun a b ha hb => ?_)
    · obtain ⟨y1, hy1, e1⟩ := exists_lift_pow hφ k a ha
      obtain ⟨y2, e2⟩ := pi_surjective φ hφ b
      have hy2 : y2 ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) := by
        rw [mem_augIdeal, ← aug_pi φ, e2]; exact mem_augIdeal.mp hb
      refine ⟨y1 * y2, ?_, by rw [map_mul, e1, e2]⟩
      rw [Submodule.pow_succ]; exact Submodule.mul_mem_mul hy1 hy2
    · obtain ⟨y1, hy1, e1⟩ := ha
      obtain ⟨y2, hy2, e2⟩ := hb
      exact ⟨y1 + y2, add_mem hy1 hy2, by rw [map_add, e1, e2]⟩

/-- `ℤ[F] → ℤ[G]/Δⁿ`. -/
def PsiG (n : ℕ) : ZF X →+* MonoidAlgebra ℤ G ⧸ augIdeal G ^ n :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.mk _).comp (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ)

theorem PsiG_surjective (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (n : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (PsiG φ n) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective.comp (pi_surjective φ hφ)

/-- `ker(ℤ[F] → ℤ[G]/Δⁿ) = ker π + 𝔣ⁿ`. -/
theorem ker_PsiG (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (n : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (PsiG φ n) = RingHom.ker (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ) ⊔ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n := by
  ext x
  rw [Submodule.mem_sup, RingHom.mem_ker, PsiG, RingHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  constructor
  · intro hx
    obtain ⟨y, hy, e⟩ := exists_lift_pow φ hφ n _ hx
    refine ⟨x - y, ?_, y, hy, sub_add_cancel x y⟩
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, e, sub_self]
  · rintro ⟨a, ha, b, hb, rfl⟩
    rw [map_add, RingHom.mem_ker.mp ha, zero_add]
    exact pi_pow_mem φ n b hb

/-- The span of `u (μ(r) − 1) v`, `r ∈ R0`, `u`, `v` words: the paper's `J_n`. -/
def Jspan (n : ℕ) : Submodule ℤ (A X n) :=
  Submodule.span ℤ {y | ∃ r ∈ R0, ∃ u v : FreeMonoid X,
    y = mon n u * ((muF n r : A X n) - 1) * mon n v}

variable {R0} in
theorem mon_mul_mem {n : ℕ} (u : FreeMonoid X) {y : A X n} (hy : y ∈ Jspan R0 n) :
    mon n u * y ∈ Jspan R0 n := by
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨r, hr, u', v, rfl⟩ := hy
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, u * u', v, by simp only [mon_mul, mul_assoc]⟩
  | zero => rw [mul_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [mul_add]; exact add_mem ha hb
  | smul c a _ ha => rw [mul_smul_comm]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c ha

variable {R0} in
theorem mul_mon_mem {n : ℕ} (v : FreeMonoid X) {y : A X n} (hy : y ∈ Jspan R0 n) :
    y * mon n v ∈ Jspan R0 n := by
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
    obtain ⟨r, hr, u, v', rfl⟩ := hy
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, u, v' * v, by simp only [mon_mul, mul_assoc]⟩
  | zero => rw [zero_mul]; exact zero_mem _
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [add_mul]; exact add_mem ha hb
  | smul c a _ ha => rw [smul_mul_assoc]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c ha

variable {R0} in
theorem Jspan_mul_left {n : ℕ} (a : A X n) {y : A X n} (hy : y ∈ Jspan R0 n) :
    a * y ∈ Jspan R0 n := by
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
  induction z using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, zero_mul]; exact zero_mem _
  | add f g hf hg => rw [map_add, add_mul]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | single w c =>
    rw [single_eq_smul, map_zsmul, smul_mul_assoc]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c (mon_mul_mem w hy)

variable {R0} in
theorem Jspan_mul_right {n : ℕ} (a : A X n) {y : A X n} (hy : y ∈ Jspan R0 n) :
    y * a ∈ Jspan R0 n := by
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective a
  induction z using MonoidAlgebra.induction_linear with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, mul_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  | add f g hf hg => rw [map_add, mul_add]; exact add_mem hf hg
  | single w c =>
    rw [single_eq_smul, map_zsmul, mul_smul_comm]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ c (mul_mon_mem w hy)

/-- `J_n` as a two-sided ideal of `A_n`. -/
def Jideal (n : ℕ) : Ideal (A X n) where
  carrier := Jspan R0 n
  add_mem' := add_mem
  zero_mem' := zero_mem _
  smul_mem' c _ hx := Jspan_mul_left c hx

instance Jideal_isTwoSided (n : ℕ) : (Jideal R0 n).IsTwoSided :=
  ⟨fun b ha => Jspan_mul_right b ha⟩

variable {R0} in
theorem mem_Jideal {n : ℕ} {y : A X n} : y ∈ Jideal R0 n ↔ y ∈ Jspan R0 n := Iff.rfl

variable {R0} in
theorem muF_sub_one_mem_J (n : ℕ) {r : FreeGroup X} (hr : r ∈ R0) :
    (muF n r : A X n) - 1 ∈ Jideal R0 n :=
  mem_Jideal.mpr (Submodule.subset_span ⟨r, hr, 1, 1, by rw [mon_one, one_mul, mul_one]⟩)

/-- `J_n = μ(𝔯)`, with `𝔯 = relIdeal R0`. -/
theorem mem_Jideal_iff (n : ℕ) (y : A X n) :
    y ∈ Jideal R0 n ↔ ∃ x ∈ relIdeal R0, mu n x = y := by
  constructor
  · intro hy
    rw [mem_Jideal] at hy
    induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem y hy =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, u, v, rfl⟩ := hy
      refine ⟨psi (single u 1) * (of ℤ (FreeGroup X) r - 1) * psi (single v 1),
        Ideal.mul_mem_right _ _ (Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (sub_one_mem_relIdeal hr)), ?_⟩
      rw [map_mul, map_mul, mu_psi, mu_psi, mu_sub_one]
    | zero => exact ⟨0, zero_mem _, map_zero _⟩
    | add a b _ _ ha hb =>
      obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := ha
      obtain ⟨x', hx', rfl⟩ := hb
      exact ⟨x + x', add_mem hx hx', map_add _ _ _⟩
    | smul c a _ ha =>
      obtain ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩ := ha
      exact ⟨c • x, zsmul_mem hx c, map_zsmul _ c x⟩
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    rw [mem_relIdeal] at hx
    induction hx using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨r, hr, u, v, rfl⟩ := hx
      rw [map_mul, map_mul, mu_sub_one, mu_of, mu_of]
      exact Jspan_mul_right _ (Jspan_mul_left _ (muF_sub_one_mem_J n hr))
    | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact zero_mem _
    | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [map_add]; exact add_mem ha hb
    | smul c a _ ha => rw [map_zsmul]; exact zsmul_mem ha c

/-- `ℤ[F] → A_n/J_n`. -/
def PhiA (n : ℕ) : ZF X →+* A X n ⧸ Jideal R0 n :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.mk _).comp (mu n)

theorem PhiA_surjective (n : ℕ) : Function.Surjective (PhiA R0 n) :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective.comp (mu_surjective n)

/-- `ker(ℤ[F] → A_n/J_n) = 𝔯 + 𝔣ⁿ`. -/
theorem ker_PhiA (n : ℕ) :
    RingHom.ker (PhiA R0 n) = relIdeal R0 ⊔ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) ^ n := by
  ext x
  rw [Submodule.mem_sup, RingHom.mem_ker, PhiA, RingHom.comp_apply,
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, mem_Jideal_iff]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨y, hy, e⟩
    refine ⟨y, hy, x - y, ?_, add_sub_cancel y x⟩
    rw [← ker_mu, RingHom.mem_ker, map_sub, e, sub_self]
  · rintro ⟨a, ha, b, hb, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨a, ha, ?_⟩
    rw [map_add, mu_eq_zero_of_mem hb, add_zero]

theorem ker_PsiG_eq (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    (n : ℕ) : RingHom.ker (PsiG φ n) = RingHom.ker (PhiA R0 n) := by
  rw [ker_PsiG φ hφ, ker_pi_eq φ R0 hφ hker, ker_PhiA]

/-- **(c) The theorem of §3.1**: `ℤ[G]/Δⁿ ≅ A_n/J_n`. -/
def quotEquiv (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0) (n : ℕ) :
    MonoidAlgebra ℤ G ⧸ augIdeal G ^ n ≃+* A X n ⧸ Jideal R0 n :=
  ((RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (PsiG_surjective φ hφ n)).symm.trans
    (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (ker_PsiG_eq φ R0 hφ hker n))).trans
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (PhiA_surjective R0 n))

theorem quotEquiv_mk (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    (n : ℕ) (x : ZF X) :
    quotEquiv φ R0 hφ hker n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ x)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (mu n x) := by
  have e : Ideal.Quotient.mk (augIdeal G ^ n) (mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ x) = PsiG φ n x := rfl
  rw [quotEquiv, RingEquiv.trans_apply, RingEquiv.trans_apply, e,
    RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_symm_apply, Ideal.quotEquivOfEq_mk,
    RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective_apply_mk]
  rfl

/-- The isomorphism sends `g = φ(w)` to `μ(w)`. -/
theorem quotEquiv_mk_of (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    (n : ℕ) (w : FreeGroup X) :
    quotEquiv φ R0 hφ hker n (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (of ℤ G (φ w))) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (muF n w : A X n) := by
  rw [← pi_of, quotEquiv_mk, mu_of]

/-- **Corollary**: `φ(w) ∈ D_n(G) ⟺ μ(w) − 1 ∈ J_n`. -/
theorem mem_D_iff (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    (n : ℕ) (w : FreeGroup X) :
    φ w ∈ D n G ↔ (muF n w : A X n) - 1 ∈ Jideal R0 n := by
  have h1 : φ w ∈ D n G ↔ of ℤ (FreeGroup X) w - 1 ∈ RingHom.ker (PsiG φ n) := by
    rw [mem_D, RingHom.mem_ker, PsiG, RingHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, map_sub,
      map_one, pi_of]
  have h2 : of ℤ (FreeGroup X) w - 1 ∈ RingHom.ker (PhiA R0 n) ↔
      (muF n w : A X n) - 1 ∈ Jideal R0 n := by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker, PhiA, RingHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, mu_sub_one]
  rw [h1, ker_PsiG_eq φ R0 hφ hker n, h2]

/-- The corollary for the presented group `⟨X | R0⟩`. -/
theorem mem_D_presented (n : ℕ) (w : FreeGroup X) :
    PresentedGroup.mk R0 w ∈ D n (PresentedGroup R0) ↔ (muF n w : A X n) - 1 ∈ Jideal R0 n :=
  mem_D_iff _ R0 (PresentedGroup.mk_surjective R0)
    (by ext x; exact MonoidHom.mem_ker.trans PresentedGroup.mk_eq_one_iff) n w

/-! ## (d) Finiteness, and exactness modulo `p^E` -/

/-- `q^{n−1} A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n` when `x^q = 1` on `G`. -/
theorem pow_smul_pos_mem_J (hφ : Function.Surjective φ)
    (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0) {q : ℕ} (hexp : ∀ g : G, g ^ q = 1) (n : ℕ)
    {y : A X n} (hy : y ∈ Pk n 1) : (q ^ (n - 1)) • y ∈ Jideal R0 n := by
  obtain ⟨z, hz, rfl⟩ := mem_Pk.mp hy
  rcases n with _ | m
  · have h0 : Ideal.Quotient.mk (Itr X 0) z = 0 :=
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (mem_Ik_zero z)
    rw [h0, smul_zero]; exact zero_mem _
  · have h1 : psi z ∈ augIdeal (FreeGroup X) := by
      have := psi_Ik hz
      rwa [Submodule.pow_one] at this
    have h2 : mapDomainRingHom ℤ φ (psi z) ∈ augIdeal G := by
      rw [mem_augIdeal, aug_pi]; exact mem_augIdeal.mp h1
    have h3 := TraceReplay.pow_smul_mem hexp m _ h2
    have h4 : ((q ^ m : ℕ) : ℤ) • psi z ∈ RingHom.ker (PsiG φ (m + 1)) := by
      rw [RingHom.mem_ker, PsiG, RingHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, map_zsmul]
      exact h3
    rw [ker_PsiG_eq φ R0 hφ hker, RingHom.mem_ker, PhiA, RingHom.comp_apply,
      Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, map_zsmul, mu_psi, Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul ℤ] at h4
    simpa using h4

end Group

/-- Exactness modulo a power of `p`, abstractly: if `P` is killed by some `p^k` modulo `J` and
`p^E P ⊆ J + p^{E+1} P`, then `p^E P ⊆ J`. -/
theorem exact_of_bounded {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] (P J : AddSubgroup M) (p E : ℕ)
    (hb : ∃ k, ∀ y ∈ P, p ^ k • y ∈ J)
    (hX : ∀ y ∈ P, ∃ j ∈ J, ∃ z ∈ P, p ^ E • y = j + p ^ (E + 1) • z) :
    ∀ y ∈ P, p ^ E • y ∈ J := by
  have step : ∀ m : ℕ, ∀ y ∈ P, ∃ j ∈ J, ∃ z ∈ P, p ^ E • y = j + p ^ (E + m + 1) • z := by
    intro m
    induction m with
    | zero => simpa using hX
    | succ m ih =>
      intro y hy
      obtain ⟨j, hj, z, hz, e⟩ := ih y hy
      obtain ⟨j', hj', z', hz', e'⟩ := hX z hz
      refine ⟨j + p ^ (m + 1) • j', add_mem hj (nsmul_mem hj' _), z', hz', ?_⟩
      have h1 : p ^ (E + m + 1) • z = p ^ (m + 1) • (p ^ E • z) := by
        rw [smul_smul, ← pow_add, show m + 1 + E = E + m + 1 by omega]
      have h2 : p ^ (m + 1) • (p ^ (E + 1) • z') = p ^ (E + (m + 1) + 1) • z' := by
        rw [smul_smul, ← pow_add, show m + 1 + (E + 1) = E + (m + 1) + 1 by omega]
      have : p ^ (E + m + 1) • z = p ^ (m + 1) • j' + p ^ (E + (m + 1) + 1) • z' := by
        rw [h1, e', smul_add, h2]
      rw [e, this]; abel
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hb
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨j, hj, z, hz, e⟩ := step k y hy
  rw [e]
  refine add_mem hj ?_
  rw [show E + k + 1 = (E + 1) + k by omega, pow_add, mul_smul]
  exact nsmul_mem (hk z hz) _

section Exact

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] (φ : FreeGroup X →* G) (R0 : Set (FreeGroup X))

/-- **(d), exactness**: if `G` has exponent dividing `p^N` and `p^E A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺`,
then `p^E A_n⁺ ⊆ J_n`. (The paper's `E` is `E + 1` here.) -/
theorem exact_mod_p (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    {p N : ℕ} (hexp : ∀ g : G, g ^ (p ^ N) = 1) (n E : ℕ)
    (hX : ∀ y ∈ Pk n 1, ∃ j ∈ Jideal R0 n, ∃ z ∈ Pk n 1, p ^ E • y = j + p ^ (E + 1) • z) :
    ∀ y ∈ Pk n 1, p ^ E • y ∈ Jideal R0 n :=
  exact_of_bounded (Pk (X := X) n 1).toAddSubgroup (Jideal R0 n).toAddSubgroup p E
    ⟨N * (n - 1), fun y hy => by
      rw [pow_mul]; exact pow_smul_pos_mem_J φ R0 hφ hker hexp n hy⟩ hX

/-- **(d), exact membership**: under the hypothesis of `exact_mod_p`, for `y ∈ A_n⁺`,
`y ∈ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺ ⟺ y ∈ J_n`. -/
theorem mem_J_iff_mod_p (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    {p N : ℕ} (hexp : ∀ g : G, g ^ (p ^ N) = 1) (n E : ℕ)
    (hX : ∀ y ∈ Pk n 1, ∃ j ∈ Jideal R0 n, ∃ z ∈ Pk n 1, p ^ E • y = j + p ^ (E + 1) • z)
    (y : A X n) :
    (∃ j ∈ Jideal R0 n, ∃ z ∈ Pk n 1, y = j + p ^ (E + 1) • z) ↔ y ∈ Jideal R0 n := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨j, hj, z, hz, rfl⟩
    refine add_mem hj ?_
    rw [pow_succ', mul_smul]
    exact nsmul_mem (exact_mod_p φ R0 hφ hker hexp n E hX z hz) _
  · intro hy
    exact ⟨y, hy, 0, zero_mem _, by rw [smul_zero, add_zero]⟩

/-- **(c) + (d), end to end**: under the hypotheses of `exact_mod_p`,
`φ w ∈ D_n(G) ⟺ μ(w) − 1 ∈ J_n + p^{E+1} A_n⁺`. -/
theorem mem_D_iff_mod_p (hφ : Function.Surjective φ) (hker : φ.ker = Subgroup.normalClosure R0)
    {p N : ℕ} (hexp : ∀ g : G, g ^ (p ^ N) = 1) (n E : ℕ)
    (hX : ∀ y ∈ Pk n 1, ∃ j ∈ Jideal R0 n, ∃ z ∈ Pk n 1, p ^ E • y = j + p ^ (E + 1) • z)
    (w : FreeGroup X) :
    φ w ∈ D n G ↔
      ∃ j ∈ Jideal R0 n, ∃ z ∈ Pk n 1, (muF n w : A X n) - 1 = j + p ^ (E + 1) • z := by
  rw [mem_D_iff φ R0 hφ hker, mem_J_iff_mod_p φ R0 hφ hker hexp n E hX]

end Exact

/-! ## (d) `Δ/Δⁿ` is finite, and a `p`-group for a finite `p`-group -/

section Finite

variable {G : Type*} [Group G]

/-- `p^{N(n−1)} Δ ⊆ Δⁿ` when `G` has exponent dividing `p^N`. -/
theorem pow_smul_aug_mem_of_exponent {p N : ℕ} (hexp : ∀ g : G, g ^ (p ^ N) = 1) (n : ℕ)
    {y : MonoidAlgebra ℤ G} (hy : y ∈ augIdeal G) :
    ((p ^ (N * (n - 1)) : ℕ) : ℤ) • y ∈ augIdeal G ^ n := by
  have h := TraceReplay.pow_smul_mem hexp (n - 1) y hy
  rw [← pow_mul] at h
  exact Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (by omega) h

/-- A finite `p`-group has exponent dividing `p^N` for some `N`. -/
theorem exponent_of_isPGroup {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [Finite G] (hG : IsPGroup p G) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ g : G, g ^ (p ^ N) = 1 := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := IsPGroup.iff_card.mp hG
  exact ⟨N, fun g => by rw [← hN]; exact pow_card_eq_one'⟩

variable (G) in
/-- `Δ/Δⁿ` as an abelian group (a quotient of `ℤ`-modules). -/
abbrev augQuot (n : ℕ) :=
  (augIdeal G).restrictScalars ℤ ⧸
    ((augIdeal G ^ n).restrictScalars ℤ).comap ((augIdeal G).restrictScalars ℤ).subtype

/-- **(d)** For a finite group `G`, `Δ/Δⁿ` is finite (it is killed by `|G|^{n−1}`). -/
theorem finite_augQuot [Finite G] (n : ℕ) : Finite (augQuot G n) := by
  refine Module.finite_of_fg_torsion _ fun y => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ y
  have hc : ((Nat.card G ^ (n - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ) ≠ 0 :=
    Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr (pow_pos Nat.card_pos _).ne'
  refine ⟨⟨((Nat.card G ^ (n - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ), mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_ne_zero hc⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [Submonoid.smul_def, ← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  show ((Nat.card G ^ (n - 1) : ℕ) : ℤ) • (y : MonoidAlgebra ℤ G) ∈ augIdeal G ^ n
  exact Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (by omega)
    (TraceReplay.pow_smul_mem (fun g => pow_card_eq_one') (n - 1) _ y.2)

/-- For a finite `p`-group `G`, `Δ` is killed by a power of `p` modulo `Δⁿ`. -/
theorem pow_smul_aug_mem_of_isPGroup {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [Finite G] (hG : IsPGroup p G)
    (n : ℕ) : ∃ k : ℕ, ∀ y ∈ augIdeal G, ((p ^ k : ℕ) : ℤ) • y ∈ augIdeal G ^ n := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exponent_of_isPGroup hG
  exact ⟨N * (n - 1), fun y hy => pow_smul_aug_mem_of_exponent hN n hy⟩

/-- **(d)** For a finite `p`-group `G`, `Δ/Δⁿ` is a finite `p`-group: finite, and killed by a
power of `p`. -/
theorem augQuot_isPGroup {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] [Finite G] (hG : IsPGroup p G) (n : ℕ) :
    Finite (augQuot G n) ∧ ∃ k : ℕ, ∀ y : augQuot G n, ((p ^ k : ℕ) : ℤ) • y = 0 := by
  refine ⟨finite_augQuot n, ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := pow_smul_aug_mem_of_isPGroup hG n
  refine ⟨k, fun y => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Submodule.Quotient.mk_surjective _ y
  rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  show ((p ^ k : ℕ) : ℤ) • (y : MonoidAlgebra ℤ G) ∈ augIdeal G ^ n
  exact hk _ y.2

end Finite

end

